 but I beg you  to stick with it you will be so glad you  did  life is strange average is 85 out of 100  across all reviews I've seen are you  going to try it let me know your  thoughts below please over on the ps3  we'll see of this obviously pop up  long time ago back in 1890 a huge chasm  has opened up in a town with endless  supplies of weird and wonderful enemies  filling out pack and flush your way  through them going down deeper into the  void using fighting mechanics described  by the creators as smash bros meet  street fighter hmm that's not all so  good old procedurally generated  environments will keep the game feeling  fresh and unique the highest score I  could find for this one was eight out of  ten from Eurogamer and metacritic has  this one at 69 out of 100 game number  four is WRC 5 last year's World Rally  Championship game I'm not the greatest  person to ask about driving games as  Super Mario Kart was the pinnacle of my  racing careers it seems solid enough  please help me out here if you've played  this type of game or you know about this  theory please give us a review below is  it worth our time or should we avoid  this one like the plague over to the  Vita for our final two games which  should be available on a ps4 to neon  chrome is a run-of-the-mill top-down  twin-stick shooter which plays in a  similar vein to Smash TV if you're as  old as me or hotline Miami the  environment has many destructible  elements which makes observing your  surroundings imperative the gameplay  does feel meaty and the enemy placements  are well thought out and every five also  flaws you complete will bring you to a  boss fight twin-stick shooters play so  well on the Vita so I'll be grabbing  this one what about you game number six  is your puzzle title for the month in  which you play as a chameleon sneaking  through levels without being spotted  this one is perfect for a bus or train  journey as levels are quite short and  beating your best time can be quite  addictive you can even channel your  inner solid snake by hiding in boxes  metacritic has this one at 71% if you  don't go in expecting too much I think  you'll enjoy this one so that's it  that's our six offering for PS Plus for  June 2017 I'm extremely happy with this  month's offering especially the ps4 game  and I can't resist the charm of neon  chrome on my beloved Vita but enough  about me what are you grabbing please  let me know your thoughts and maybe  consider pushing that like button if  this video helps and come subscribe if  you haven't joined our dysfunctional  family already that is anyway I'm Adam  from Playstation grenade it's been a  pleasure I'll see you next time  [Music]

